<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the main app in a Developer ID build with a provisioning profile (ADR-0045).

  macOS lists a credential provider extension under System Settings > General > AutoFill &
  Passwords > "AutoFill from" (and offers it in Safari) only when BOTH the extension AND its
  containing app carry `com.apple.developer.authentication-services.autofill-credential-provider`.
  Measured on macOS 27 (26A428): SafariFoundation's SFCredentialProviderExtensionManager filters
  every discovered extension through `extensionAndContainingAppHaveDeveloperEntitlement`, which
  reads the entitlement from the extension's plug-in record and from the containing app's
  LSBundleRecord. With the entitlement on the extension only, pluginkit reports it registered and
  enabled, yet Settings shows only Apple Passwords.

  The entitlement is restricted, so the app then needs its own Developer ID provisioning profile:
  App ID com.kagisecure.app with the "AutoFill Credential Provider" capability. Otherwise this file
  matches Signing/App.entitlements (sandbox off, the App Group).

  The application-identifier, team-identifier and keychain-access-groups keys (all permitted by the
  profile) let the app own Secure Enclave keychain items, which live in the data-protection
  keychain: without them SecItemAdd fails with errSecMissingEntitlement and Touch ID unlock is
  unavailable (ADR-0011, amended 2026-10-04).
  `make macos SIGN=developer-id` and `cargo xtask dist` select it through KAGI_APP_ENTITLEMENTS
  and KAGI_APP_PROFILE (APP_PROFILE / KAGISECURE_APP_PROFILE to use another profile name).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<false/>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.kagisecure</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
	<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.kagisecure.app</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
	<string>4CZNJKU58K</string>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)com.kagisecure.app</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.authentication-services.autofill-credential-provider</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
